  "summary": "Comparing genomes tied the 2026 cruise ship outbreak to a 2018 outbreak in Argentina and to a single Andes virus lineage seen in northern Patagonia through 2025. The 2018 outbreak may also have involved person-to-person spread, but there was no sign of widespread community transmission. Travel routes of the first cases did not fit the expected incubation period, so the actual source remains unresolved.",
